    summary: "Hydrogen is the chemical element with the symbol H and atomic number 1. It is the most abundant chemical substance in the universe.", 
    details: "Hydrogen is the most abundant chemical substance in the universe, constituting roughly 75% of all baryonic mass. Non-remnant stars are mainly composed of hydrogen in the plasma state.\n\n### Characteristics\nAt standard temperature and pressure, hydrogen is a colorless, odorless, tasteless, non-toxic, nonmetallic, highly combustible diatomic gas with the molecular formula H2. Hydrogen also happens to be the lightest element in the periodic table. Its most common isotope, protium, consists of a single proton and no neutrons.\n\n### Scientific Significance\nThe development of the quantum mechanical theory of the atomic structure of hydrogen played a key role in the history of science. Because it is the simplest atom, it has been a primary subject of study in physics and chemistry.\n\n### Industrial Applications\nIn industry, hydrogen is used primarily for the processing of fossil fuels (e.g., hydrocracking) and the production of ammonia for fertilizers. More recently, hydrogen has gained significant attention as a clean energy carrier. Fuel cells can convert hydrogen and oxygen into electricity with water as the only byproduct, offering a potential path for decarbonizing transportation and heavy industry.",
