    summary: "Boron is a low-abundance element in the Solar System and in the Earth's crust. It is a metalloid found in various compounds, notably borate minerals.", 
    details: "Boron is a chemical element with the symbol B and atomic number 5. Because boron is produced entirely by cosmic ray spallation and supernovae and not by stellar nucleosynthesis, it is a low-abundance element in the Solar System and in the Earth's crust.\n\n### Characteristics\nPure boron is a dark, amorphous powder. Crystalline boron is very hard, black, and lustrous. It is a semiconductor, meaning its electrical conductivity increases with temperature. Boron is chemically similar to silicon in its ability to form stable covalent networks.\n\n### Industrial Applications\nThe most important compounds of boron are boric acid, borax, and boron oxide. These are used in the manufacture of glass and ceramics, particularly heat-resistant borosilicate glass (like Pyrex). Boron is also used as a dopant in the semiconductor industry and in the production of high-strength materials like boron fibers.\n\n### Biological Role\nWhile boron is an essential micronutrient for plants, its role in human health is less clearly defined but is thought to be involved in bone maintenance and brain function. It is naturally present in many fruits, vegetables, and nuts.\n\n### Fun Fact\nAmorphous boron is used in pyrotechnic flares to provide a distinctive green color, and in rockets as an igniter.",
