    summary: "Oxygen is the chemical element with the symbol O and atomic number 8. It is a highly reactive nonmetal and oxidizing agent.", 
    details: "Oxygen is the third-most abundant element in the universe, after hydrogen and helium. At standard temperature and pressure, two atoms of the element bind to form dioxygen, a colorless and odorless gas with the formula O2.\n\n### Biological Role\nOxygen is essential for aerobic respiration in most living organisms. It is also a key component of organic molecules such as proteins, nucleic acids, and carbohydrates. Photosynthesis by plants and algae provides the majority of the oxygen in Earth's atmosphere.\n\n### Industrial and Medical Applications\nOxygen is used in the production of steel, plastics and textiles, as well as for brazing, welding and cutting of steel and other metals. Oxygen therapy is used to treat patients with respiratory conditions and as part of life support systems in aircraft, submarines, spaceflight and diving.\n\n### Ozone\nOzone (O3) is an allotrope of oxygen that is highly reactive and forms a protective layer in the upper atmosphere, absorbing harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun.",
