    summary: "Phosphorus is a chemical element that exists in two main forms: white phosphorus and red phosphorus. It is vital for life as a component of DNA and ATP.", 
    details: "Phosphorus is a chemical element with the symbol P and atomic number 15. Because of its high reactivity, phosphorus is never found as a free element on Earth.\n\n### Allotropes\nThe two most common allotropes of phosphorus are white phosphorus and red phosphorus. White phosphorus is a waxy solid that is highly toxic and self-ignites in air, glowing with a faint green light (chemiluminescence). Red phosphorus is non-toxic, more stable, and is used on the striking surface of matchboxes.\n\n### Biological Importance\nPhosphorus is an essential constituent of life. It forms the structural backbone of DNA and RNA. Living cells also use phosphorus to transport cellular energy via adenosine triphosphate (ATP), which is vital for every living process. It is also a key component of phospholipids, which form all cell membranes, and calcium phosphate, which provides strength to bones and teeth.\n\n### Agricultural and Industrial Uses\nThe vast majority of phosphorus produced is used in agriculture as concentrated phosphoric acids for fertilizers. These fertilizers are crucial for maintaining high crop yields worldwide. Phosphorus is also used in the manufacture of steel, detergents, and special glasses.\n\n### Discovery\nPhosphorus was the first element discovered that was not known since ancient times. It was isolated in 1669 by the German alchemist Hennig Brand, who prepared it from urine.",
