    details: "Argon is a chemical element with the symbol Ar and atomic number 18. It is in group 18 of the periodic table and is a noble gas. Argon is the third-most abundant gas in the Earth's atmosphere, at 0.934% (9340 ppmv), making it more than twice as abundant as water vapor.\n\n### Inert Nature\nLike other noble gases, argon has a full outer shell of electrons, which makes it extremely stable and resistant to bonding with other elements. This inertness is its most valuable property in industrial applications. The name 'argon' is derived from the Greek word 'argos', meaning 'lazy' or 'inactive'.\n\n### Industrial Applications\nArgon is used frequently when an inert atmosphere is needed. It is used in this way for the production of titanium and other reactive elements. It is also used by researchers in experiments where an inert environment is required. It is commonly used as a shielding gas in arc welding and in incandescent light bulbs to prevent the filament from oxidizing.\n\n### Scientific Uses\nArgon is used in some specialized medical procedures, such as laser surgery (argon lasers), and in cryosurgery. It is also used in the potassium-argon dating method to determine the age of ancient rocks and minerals.\n\n### Earth's Crust\nNearly all of the argon in Earth's atmosphere is radiogenic argon-40, derived from the decay of potassium-40 in Earth's crust. In contrast, argon in the universe is primarily argon-36, produced by stellar nucleosynthesis.",
