    period: 4, 
    summary: "Cobalt is a hard, lustrous, silver-grey metal. It is found in the Earth's crust only in chemically combined form.", 
    details: "Cobalt is a chemical element with the symbol Co and atomic number 27. Like iron, cobalt can be magnetized and so is used to make magnets. It is alloyed with aluminum and nickel to make particularly powerful magnets called alnico.\n\n### Historical and Pigment Use\nCobalt compounds have been used for centuries to impart a rich blue color to glass, glazes and ceramics. This distinctive 'cobalt blue' is stable even at high temperatures. The name 'cobalt' comes from the German word 'kobold', meaning goblin, because medieval miners thought the ores were troublesome and poisonous.\n\n### Industrial and Superalloys\nMost cobalt is used in the production of superalloys. These are metallic alloys that are highly resistant to corrosion and high temperatures, making them ideal for gas turbine engines, aircraft components, and industrial machinery. Cobalt is also used in wear-resistant alloys for surgical implants.\n\n### Battery Technology\nIn recent years, cobalt has become a critical material in the production of lithium-ion batteries, where it is used in the cathode. This makes it vital for the electronics industry and the transition to electric vehicles.\n\n### Biological Role\nCobalt is an essential trace element for all animals as the active center of coenzymes called cobalamins, the most common of which is Vitamin B12. Humans must obtain this vitamin from animal-derived foods or supplements.",
