    period: 4, 
    summary: "Zinc is a slightly brittle metal at room temperature and has a blue-silvery appearance when oxidation is removed.", 
    details: "Zinc is a chemical element with the symbol Zn and atomic number 30. It is the first element in group 12 of the periodic table. In some respects, zinc is chemically similar to magnesium.\n\n### Galvanization\nThe most important use of zinc is in the protection of other metals, primarily iron and steel, from corrosion. This process, called galvanization, involves coating the metal with a thin layer of zinc. Zinc acts as a sacrificial anode, corroding in preference to the underlying metal.\n\n### Alloys: Brass and Bronze\nZinc is often alloyed with copper to create brass. Brass has been used by humans for thousands of years and is valued for its strength, corrosion resistance, and attractive appearance. Zinc is also a minor component in some types of bronze.\n\n### Biological Importance\nZinc is an essential trace element for humans, animals, plants, and microorganisms. It is a cofactor for over 300 enzymes and plays a vital role in immune function, protein synthesis, wound healing, DNA synthesis, and cell division. Zinc deficiency is a global health issue, particularly in developing countries.\n\n### Die Casting and Batteries\nDue to its low melting point and high fluidity, zinc is ideal for die casting intricate parts for the automotive, electrical, and hardware industries. It is also used in various types of batteries, including common alkaline batteries and zinc-carbon batteries.",
