    summary: "Terbium is a silvery-white, malleable, and ductile rare-earth metal. It is primarily used for its phosphorescent and magnetic properties.", 
    details: "Terbium is a chemical element with the symbol Tb and atomic number 65. It is a member of the lanthanide series. It is a silvery-white metal that is soft enough to be cut with a knife and is relatively stable in air.\n\n### Green Phosphors\nTerbium is widely used as a phosphor to produce a vibrant green color in various applications. It is essential for the green color in fluorescent lamps, computer monitors, and LED displays. It is also used as a dopant in x-ray screens to improve their sensitivity and image quality.\n\n### Magnetostriction and Sonar\nTerbium is a key component of Terfenol-D, an alloy that exhibits huge magnetostriction—it changes shape significantly when placed in a magnetic field. This property makes it vital for high-power sonar systems, precise acoustic actuators, and specialized sensors.\n\n### Electronics and Glass\nTerbium is used in high-performance solid-state devices and as a dopant in high-quality optical glass to improve its refractive index. It is also used in specialized alloys for aerospace and industrial applications. Some terbium compounds are used as biological probes in research.\n\n### Discovery\nTerbium was discovered in 1843 by the Swedish chemist Carl Gustaf Mosander. He identified it as a component of 'yttria,' along with erbium and yttrium. Like yttrium, erbium, and ytterbium, it was named after the Ytterby mine in Sweden.",
