    period: 9, 
    summary: "Holmium is a relatively soft and malleable silvery-white rare-earth metal. It possesses the highest magnetic strength of any element.", 
    details: "Holmium is a chemical element with the symbol Ho and atomic number 67. It is a member of the lanthanide series. Holmium has the highest magnetic moment of any naturally occurring element and possesses other unusual magnetic properties.\n\n### Extreme Magnetic Strength\nDue to its record-high magnetic moment, holmium is used to create the strongest artificially generated static magnetic fields when placed as a magnetic pole piece in high-power magnets. It is also used in the manufacture of high-performance magnetic recording heads and sensors.\n\n### Laser Technology\nHolmium-doped yttrium lithium fluoride (Ho:YLF) and holmium-doped yttrium aluminum garnet (Ho:YAG) lasers produce infrared light at a wavelength that is highly absorbed by water. This makes 'holmium lasers' ideal for specialized medical and surgical procedures, such as laser lithotripsy for breaking up kidney stones and in some types of eye surgery.\n\n### Optical Filters and Glass\nHolmium oxide is used to color glass in a characteristic peach-pink shade. It is also used in specialized optical filters and as a calibration standard for spectrophotometers because it has sharp and well-defined absorption peaks across the ultraviolet and visible spectrum.\n\n### Discovery\nHolmium was discovered in 1878 by the Swiss chemists Marc Delafontaine and Jacques-Louis Soret, and independently by the Swedish chemist Per Teodor Cleve. It was named after 'Holmia,' the Latin name for the city of Stockholm.",
