    summary: "Gold is a bright, slightly reddish yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. It is one of the most precious and least reactive chemical elements.", 
    details: "Gold is unique among transition metals for its brilliant yellow color and extreme resistance to corrosion. It is found in the Earth's crust as native nuggets or grains and has been prized by humanity for millennia.\n\n### Historical Importance\nGold has been used for coinage, jewelry, and other arts throughout recorded history. In the past, a gold standard was often implemented as a monetary policy, serving as the backbone for global economies until the mid-20th century.\n\n### Physical Properties\nIn its pure form, gold is the most malleable and ductile of all metals. A single gram of gold can be beaten into a sheet of one square meter, and an ounce into a wire 80 kilometers long. It is also an excellent conductor of heat and electricity.\n\n### Industrial & Modern Uses\nBeyond its value as an investment and in jewelry, gold's high conductivity and resistance to oxidation make it indispensable in modern electronics. It is used in reliable electrical connectors for computers, smartphones, and aerospace technology. Gold is also used in infrared shielding, gold leafing for architectural decoration, and in medicine for certain specialized treatments.\n\n### Fun Fact\nAll the gold ever mined in human history would fit into a cube roughly 21 meters on each side. Despite its immense value, gold is remarkably rare in the universe compared to lighter elements.",
