    summary: "Lead is a chemical element with the symbol Pb and atomic number 82. It is a heavy metal that is denser than most common materials.", 
    details: "Lead is soft and malleable, and also has a relatively low melting point. When freshly cut, lead is silvery with a hint of blue; it tarnishes to a dull gray color when exposed to air.\n\n### Characteristics\nLead has the highest atomic number of any stable element and three of its isotopes are endpoints of major nuclear decay chains of heavier elements. Lead is a relatively unreactive post-transition metal.\n\n### Historical and Modern Uses\nLead was used in plumbing (the word 'plumbing' derives from the Latin 'plumbum' for lead), as well as in white lead paints and leaded gasoline. Today, lead is used in lead-acid batteries, ammunition, weights, and as a shield from radiation in X-ray machines and nuclear reactors.\n\n### Toxicity\nLead is a potent neurotoxin that accumulates in soft tissues and bones; it damages the nervous system and interferes with the function of biological enzymes, causing neurological disorders, such as brain damage and behavioral problems.",
