    summary: "Rutherfordium is a highly radioactive synthetic element. It is the first of the transactinide elements.", 
    details: "Rutherfordium is a chemical element with the symbol Rf and atomic number 104. It is the first of the transactinide elements and a member of the transition metal group. It was first synthesized in 1964/1969.\n\n### Transactinide Milestone\nRutherfordium marks a major transition in the periodic table, following the actinide series. It is a 6d transition metal. Its discovery was part of the 'Transfermium Wars,' with competing claims from the JINR in Russia and the LBNL in the US. Both teams successfully synthesized it using heavy-ion bombardment.\n\n### Extreme Instability\nAll isotopes of rutherfordium are highly radioactive and short-lived. The most stable known isotope, rutherfordium-267, has a half-life of only 1.3 hours. This makes it incredibly difficult to perform chemical experiments. However, scientists have successfully determined that its chemical behavior is similar to its neighbor hafnium.\n\n### Scientific Importance\nRutherfordium is studied to understand the limits of atomic stability and the behavior of the heaviest transition metals. It has no practical applications beyond basic research.\n\n### Discovery and Naming\nThe element was named after Ernest Rutherford, the 'father of nuclear physics,' who discovered the atomic nucleus and first described the radioactive decay of elements.",
