    details: "Copernicium is a chemical element with the symbol Cn and atomic number 112. It is a transactinide element and a d-block transition metal. it was first synthesized in 1996 at the GSI in Darmstadt, Germany.\n\n### Unusually Volatile Metal\nPerhaps the most fascinating property of copernicium is that it is predicted to be a volatile metal, possibly even a gas at standard temperature and pressure. This is due to extreme relativistic effects on its 6d and 7s electrons, which make it more like a noble gas (mercury-like behavior). Recent experiments on a few atoms have supported the idea and shown it to be more volatile than its neighbor mercury.\n\n### Synthesis and Discovery\nThe discovery team, led by Sigurd Hofmann, bombarded a lead-208 target with zinc-70 ions. Copernicium decays very rapidly, with its most stable isotope, copernicium-285, having a half-life of about 29 seconds.\n\n### Discovery and Naming\nCopernicium was named after the astronomer Nicolaus Copernicus, who famously proposed the heliocentric model of the solar system. The name was chosen to honor the bridge between the physical sciences and the wider understanding of the universe.",
